 them to the list and then a  HootSuite say I want to import that list  and have a custom column for it so in  this case it's my family and so this is  my sister Alexandra and I've added her  to my list and so anytime she tweets I  have it here as well I can always see  what she's up to so  you know here she says she's been having  some berries and pumpkin seeds for  dinner that's great I can write back if  I want to that's a great way to just  sustain touch and see what's happening  the next list that I made was for  business so these are some of my  business contacts that I in stay in  touch with and just see what they're up  to so Tasha David a couple more we  scroll down we can see you know more  different tweets and up to me again if I  want to stay in touch with these people  and send them a note or not just see  what they're doing and again you know  quick easy way so this is another list  that I made called business and just  business contacts that I want to stay in  touch with a lot of the business  contacts that I have aren't necessarily  on Twitter or don't have a personal  account so it may be hard to add them on  here but if they do was a great way to  just stay in touch and see what people  are up to and if you you know have a  reason to connect with somebody it's  easy to show it here through that list  so it's great idea to have different  lists for different contacts some of  them maybe more important than others  and so to make sure you don't lose the  stream of people that you're connecting  with you can easily import your list  into here the next thing you can do is  also do it based on keywords so the  first two lists one was from my family  one is for business the next thing that  I have here is for certain keywords so  this is usually I set this up for  keywords that I'm tracking usually for  people who want to be on Twitter or  should be on Twitter I've kind of  convinced them to join but they're not  sold on the idea yet so I've helped them 